{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20","id":1539998,"title":"What V5 Mechanics Would/Do You Port to V20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-07T10:59:52-07:00","id":1539998,"title":"What V5 Mechanics Would/Do You Port to V20?","content":"There are things in V5 that I like, but I am considering revisiting V20.<br /> <br /> What components of V5 would you bring to V20?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T12:02:40-07:00","id":1540003,"title":"","content":"I'd personally resist the urge to port anything, mostly because I know I would make this more complex and time consuming than it needs to be, and in general I prefer to just go for Requiem when I want better rules.<br /> <br /> That said, I really like how V5 did Hunger and Hunger Dice, and I probably will try to implement it and ditch Blood Points in future games. Maybe even in VtR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T13:27:24-07:00","id":1540007,"title":"","content":"I think the concepts of coterie types and feeding types are interesting and so I\u2019ve conceptually cribbed from those although I don\u2019t use the V5 mechanics associated with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T08:49:20-07:00","id":1540043,"title":"","content":"Hunger dice, lore sheets, merged disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T10:44:48-07:00","id":1540050,"title":"","content":"None. While there are some appealing rules in V5 to consider, I've found better versions of pretty much every one of them in other games to pull from instead<br /> <br /> VtR1e's Atrocity Dice optional rules are something I find more appealing. BtP's feeding and Satiety system make juggling hunger and feeding a lot more engaging where the players want to engage with risks of different feeding strategies on their own instead of it just being about dice; BtP's 'some powers get stronger when you're hungry and some get stronger when you're full,' balancing act also makes concepts like predatory archetypes more organic.<br /> <br /> Loresheets lifted things so directly from Weapon of the Gods that it's kinda painfully obvious they didn't really consider how to adapt them to the different setting conceits. Loresheets would be drastically improved (they aren't exactly state of the art game design in their original form) by adding the Introduce Facts mechanics from Exalted 3e with the first function of a Loresheet to be an area of the setting your character can introduce facts from (in the original WofG implementation, regardless of what perks you spend points on from your Loresheet, you automatically gain extensive knowledge on whatever the subject is, so even if you put zero points into a Loresheet, your character was still an academic/theoretical expert on the subject). Loresheets would also benefit a lot from a more standardized way to determining what they can get you so it's easier for long time VtM fans to build appropriate ones. CofD 2e's Mystery Cult Initiation, Vigil 2e's Endowments, or the Storypath Path Connections models could all do well in helping making Loresheets that feel far more in-line with what the original concept was supposed to do.<br /> <br /> So, if I just had V20 and V5, I could see myself doing some pulling from V5 for V20. But having a much larger gaming library to pull rules from for tinkering, I've seen a lot more appealing stuff out there (even with my examples above not even leaving the ST family of games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T11:21:58-07:00","id":1540053,"title":"","content":"The way Attributes and Skills are assigned in character creation, and that's pretty much it. And that's if I'm not either porting it to Requiem 2e or just running Requiem 2e instead. There have been significant updates and reworkings of the original Storyteller system (Revised Storyteller, Storyteller Revised, Storytelling, Storytelling 2e, Storypath), and WoD5 mostly feels like another crack at Storytelling 1e.<br /> <br /> Even Loresheets are to me worse versions of those in Legends of the Wulin or Paths from Storypath. Even Fate's Aspects are a much more powerful tool for establishing ties to a setting. It certainly doesn't help that they can implicitly limit the kinds of relationships you can have with their associated characters or groups.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day if I'm playing WoD20 and I want better rules I have a lot more options than stealing from V5. Even it's nearest addition of Hunger Dice needs IMO a reworking or vastly refocused system to be viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T21:57:40-07:00","id":1541947,"title":"","content":"Completely reject the generation dynamic.<br /> <br /> You know, like Requiem.<br /> <br /> And also, get rid of Path of Conjuration. That's just nonsensical, that a vampire can summon literally anything from blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T13:56:36-07:00","id":1541987,"title":"","content":"The generation theme is a defined part of VTM lore and ensures endless conflict as there's going to be a kindred with greater mystical power and there would be others that will covet it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T01:17:29-07:00","id":1542034,"title":"","content":"There are several mechanics I like about V5 although I'm not a fan of it overall<br /> <br /> - Assigning points to attributes and skills. Easy to adapt and gives more flexibility<br /> - Predator Types. An excellent concept but difficult to port thanks to it being an integral part of character creation<br /> - Touchstones and Convictions. Good for roleplay, easy to port as an rp element but you have to drop all the dice rolls around it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T04:44:28-07:00","id":1542039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1540050#post1540050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...juggling hunger and feeding a lot more engaging where the players want to engage with risks of different feeding strategies on their own instead of it just being about dice...</div> </div> </div> </div>This applies to every edition, but feeding is a tricky endeavor to adjudicate -- not difficult, just tricky -- at its best times. You have to balance what's on the session's agenda with player interest and experience with the system/setting, needs of the story, all while leaving wiggle room for complication and minor derail. How to balance &quot;personal horror&quot; with players simply getting bored/desensitized has been a subject discussed to death elsewhere. At the end of the day, regardless of system it's going to have to be accomplished on a per-table basis with room for adaptation as needs dictate.<br /> <br /> My old in-person group played Vampire enough to know what's up, which means &quot;just roll and if you pooch it we'll go from there&quot; does the trick. Lengthy feeding scenes just bored them because they'd all been there and done that, and wanted to get on with the main plot. If nothing else running a feeding scene for the sake of just doing a feeding scene, made them innately suspicious and eager to run down whatever red herring they decided (completely on their own) I wanted them to focus on.<br /> <br /> Half of my new group was new to Vampire, which left a lot more breathing room to run feeding scenes for everyone to get their heads in the game and in-character, familiarize everyone with game mechanics, and help reinforce setting and theme. It didn't take long for them to pick up on it enough to start short-handing little things, which is important to build that foundation and start going deeper on setting/theme. It was a nice change for me as a storyteller, to revisit old (to me) topics long taken for granted.<br /> <br /> Where V5 goes simultaneously wrong and right, is establishing rules and an idea springboard for the variety of ways a vampire <i>can</i> feed outside norms established by popular culture. And by extension/implication, how certain advantages, flaws, and disciplines correspond to feeding methods. But...the authors could have done a lot better to establish predator type isn't a restriction, it's a <i>preference</i> (with certain clan/merit/flaw-based constraint).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T19:34:14-07:00","id":1542085,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, you quoted me talking about the CofD game Beast: the Primordial. It uses an entirely different &quot;hunger and feeding&quot; mechanics than any edition of Vampire has so far.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I've been tempted to use it as the base for a vampire game (besides the struggle of finding groups comfortable dealing with Beast's baggage), is the whole concept is better oriented towards avoiding so many of the issues you brought up. BtP feeding is done at the end of a scene with one roll based on everything that happened (if you did enough to even get a roll) so it doesn't derail the scene itself to stop and figure out how much hunger you deal with in the middle of play. It's very player driven regarding how complicated things can get, so the level of horror in a given scene is on the players to decide on more than the ST. <br /> <br /> It also helps a lot by not having any &quot;good&quot; state to be in. There are two &quot;bad&quot; states and three &quot;mixed bag&quot; states. Characters naturally orient towards one of the three mixed bag states as their default because it best suits how the character tries to balance the needs of their hunger and how they try to justify what they do to feed themselves. There's no strong moral aspect to this either. The most hungry of the three main states is appealing to brutish monsters for how strongly it empowers the Begotten's more direct powers, but it's also appealing to characters trying to be ethical via harm reduction as it has the lowest feeding restrictions. The high satiety state lets you be subtle and cautious in your approach as you grow far more potent with powers that control people by hijacking their nightmares, but with the highest feeding restrictions these can easily be the most noxious Beasts because of how much damage they have to do each time they feed in comparison and they can be more detached from people so they can arrange their meals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T05:27:50-07:00","id":1542109,"title":"","content":"I imported touchstones as a background trait, effectively they'd provide and xp reduction to humanity purchases per dot to a min of 2. But if one died you made a degeneration role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-14T15:12:36-07:00","id":1542140,"title":"","content":"So... you imported a VtR 2e rule and modified it? Touchstones as originated in VtR were a background (though CofD had already combined Merits and Backgrounds into the same trait group) where you increased it to have more of them. V5 cut out that part of the VtR implementation to tie Touchstones to Convictions instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-15T14:54:12-07:00","id":1542203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542109#post1542109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imported touchstones as a background trait, effectively they'd provide and xp reduction to humanity purchases per dot to a min of 2. But if one died you made a degeneration role.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this I don't have a problem with. I never liked Touchstones because they were mandatory. A stick used to force the player to engage with the specific themes the designers had in mind. Rather than as a carrot, an opt-in system that REWARDS the player for doing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T00:16:33-07:00","id":1542232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542203#post1542203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See, this I don't have a problem with. I never liked Touchstones because they were mandatory. A stick used to force the player to engage with the specific themes the designers had in mind. Rather than as a carrot, an opt-in system that REWARDS the player for doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problem in 5th is touchstones are misused as a railroading device rather than a roleplay tool. You're effectively forced to write npcs your pc 'cares' about and they're explicitly muggles since the writters think that makes it more grounded. One of the few times i flipped the figurative table with a game was when a gm nagged me over the entire of session 0 into having a human bff just to make it pregnant with a super wyrm antichrist and i was expected to go through lots of angst and conflict for it. He was upset when i just killed the npc and burnt the feutus because i was playing a shadow lord and just spent an ic weekend mourning her.<br /> <br /> Touchstones feel a lot like that. A lot of potential lousy execution","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T01:37:25-07:00","id":1542236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542232#post1542232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of potential lousy execution</div> </div> </div> </div>That pretty much sums up my feelings about V5 (but please don't take that as encouragement to turn this into an anti-V5 thread)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T01:40:29-07:00","id":1542237,"title":"","content":"I do like some concepts in V5, like Hunger dice for example and I appreciate that it's easier for 2 identical clans to be more obvious in their differences on paper but overall I don't like it enough to bring it in to my V20 games. I am not very experienced with V5 so more of it may grow on me but overall I'd say none for now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27150-minnzy","name":"Minnzy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T12:34:06-07:00","id":1542263,"title":"","content":"What would i port to V20?<br /> <br /> Some of he Auxiliary Physical discipline powers, like a more powerful jump for Potence, and good lord Fortitude needs buffing - i would apply it to most Stamina-related pools even mental tasks. Celerity...doesnt need much because it could be abused very easily. <br /> <br /> Touchstones are good ideas for more defined character plot points but i would implement them differently. Basic over-arching character goals and things that relate to their Humanity which they have to defend. <br /> <br /> Not a mechanic per se, but consolidating some Clans and Bloodlines is good, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T23:12:11-07:00","id":1542296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542034#post1542034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Predator Types. An excellent concept but difficult to port thanks to it being an integral part of character creation</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a big fan of having Predator Type being a part of character creation, but I like having defined roles for more types of hunting.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T02:48:41-07:00","id":1542302,"title":"","content":"Predator types as implemented suffer because they have massive impacts on character creation (and not balanced ones in terms of relative XP costs), and then have no substantive impact in play. They're nice as both player-to-ST communication (it's a quick way to say a lot about your character's night-to-night activities) and they're nice RP aids, but there's nothing stopping players form picking a type for the mechanics and never really feeding that way in play; there's no carrot or stick about it.<br /> <br /> If I was going to just port them into V20, I'd do something like have them replace Demeanor (a trait that's basically fluff as it is) in character creation (so players are thinking about it, and it does do the communication part effectively), and then have some small bonus like +1 vitae per scene or per downtime feeding roll if you feed appropriately to your type. All of the char-gen Discipline, Humanity, and Background/Merit/Flaw adjustments really don't help them do their job in the game. It also lets them be more customizable. There's a big different between a Nosferatu or Gangrel that feeds on animals by default out of practicality vs. a vampire that does it for moral/Humanity reasons when they don't face any particular issues being around normal humans to hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T05:24:42-07:00","id":1542306,"title":"","content":"I think lore sheets are really cool, but that's about it personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T07:56:31-07:00","id":1542312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542302#post1542302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator types as implemented suffer because they have massive impacts on character creation (and not balanced ones in terms of relative XP costs), and then have no substantive impact in play. They're nice as both player-to-ST communication (it's a quick way to say a lot about your character's night-to-night activities) and they're nice RP aids, but there's nothing stopping players form picking a type for the mechanics and never really feeding that way in play; there's no carrot or stick about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they have substantial impact on character creation -- it's a part of it, incorporated with backstory, character typing, and theme. It <i>should</i>.<br /> <br /> Predator types with highly niche feeding styles -- farmer, graverobber/bagger, grim reaper, consensualist, trapdoor, blood leech -- lean more heavily into facilitating those styles while enforcing restrictions on characters who choose them. I don't see how there's no carrot or stick, when many predator types heavily restrict potential vessels, up to and including nominal inability to feed (or extreme cost of feeding) on mortals at all. Those also happen to be the predator types an enterprising player might select for mechanics, since they grant dots in uncommon disciplines (namely, protean and oblivion) or an additional blood potency at character generation.<br /> <br /> Are other predator types less restrictive? yeah -- they're expressly intended to be. It's the distinction between generalism and specialty. The benefit to an open-ended predator type is adaptability -- both graverobbers and baggers have iron gullet and prefer cold blood, but the former will have difficulty feeding in a traditional rack whereas the latter would not.<br /> <br /> Which by extension raises the Humanity spectre -- by RAW player characters cannot raise Humanity at all, it's an <i>optional</i> rule for ST's to allow it...either through extensive, dedicated, and borderline flawless roleplay, and/or with experience at new rating times <i>ten</i>. The difference between Humanity 7 and 6 may not be huge, but far more substantial than any edition to date. And, that difference already has major implications for certain predator types (most notably, siren).<br /> <br /> Blood leech is the most munchkin-friendly predator type in the game thus far. It offers highly-valuable specialty in one of the two more valuable abilities in game, your choice in one of the two stronger disciplines in the game, an additional blood potency...at the cost of an Humanity, and two nasty flaws one of which is Prey Exclusion (mortals). And that one puts you 50 experience in the hole, as it costs 20 to buy BP 2 but would cost 70 to buy Humanity 7 (if the ST even allows it).<br /> <br /> Sure, there's also crossover between predator types, and which predator types are more appropriate based on character can be questionable. I ran into this issue myself creating a Toreador NPC for my most recent chronicle, who's a BDSM sex worker that does exclusively incall and porn. Was it more appropriate to make her a siren, scene queen, or trapdoor? any of the three would be equally valid choices. In the end, it was absolutely a mechanical choice: trapdoor's specialty, backgrounds, and flaws were more appropriate to the character, even if protean or obfuscate were facially unorthodox.<br /> <br /> Other than that, as background costs have been normalized (it's just three per dot now, unattached to current or new rating) the biggest swing one could get from a dot in predator type is...ten XP. The biggest value-add in terms of experience is starting with level 3 in a clan discipline (15 experience), and the lowest is starting with a third clan discipline at level 1 (5 experience). Value-add from starting with a first dot in an out-of-clan discipline is nominally 7, but in practice is all over the place and unquantifiable, depending on the discipline in question, its comparative value in accordance to table and type of chronicle, and whether or not that discipline dot is a prerequisite for amalgams a player may desire for their character.<br /> <br /> That's an amount of experience points that normalizes inside a single story's worth of gain. It's still a far cry from freebie points, that can be gamed to put a character up to a hundred experience ahead of another, with savvy distribution and merit/flaw selection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T13:56:38-07:00","id":1542335,"title":"","content":"It doesn't matter that the predator types have less negative impact on PC XP-value balance in V5 than V20 already has in the BP/XP divide; they introduce even more as written if you add them without modification. V5 could actually claim to have an XP balanced starting spread compared to all previous VtM editions (though VtR 2e beat it to the punch) if not for the predator types. Predator types also aren't an exhaustive unalterable list. While the list is fairly comprehensive, there's nothing stopping the ST and players from modifying them or creating new ones if something else would work better (and not just Rule Zero).<br /> <br /> As for carrots and sticks, I mean things outside of the specific pool of mechanics they offer up. If you take two characters that have to different types, but then the course of the story pushes them in the same direction and then end up with identical sheets... all differences regarding feeding are essentially erased. It's not like they offer exclusive traits or something; even if V5's high XP costs and low XP hand outs makes every extra dot at creation that much more impactful.<br /> <br /> Compared to other Vampire editions, the predator types are just taking what would normally be points to flush out a character to the player's desires, and putting them in a &quot;feeding&quot; bucket. It's extra scaffolding in terms of game design. It's not &quot;necessary&quot; but largely serves its purpose of giving more direction on what's important to think about when assigning values to your character's sheet. In V20, you can informally just ask players to explain how their character normally feeds and see if their sheet really meshes with that, and end up with largely the same outcomes; it's just not as baked in.<br /> <br /> I personally find the &quot;should&quot; statement rather odd given that V5 encourages much fresher vampires than older editions did as the default. If one of V5's goals was to make the default closer to newly embraced vampires instead of vampires with a decade or more of being undead under their belts, it makes less sense for the characters to have settled into feeding strategies so much that they can have such a drastic starting impact.<br /> <br /> Also, frankly, if you're going to try to edition war and write fanboy screeds at people every time V5 gets criticized, people aren't going to care even when you make good points. You're just sabotaging your own credibility to discuss these things reasonably. Even more so since the mods just asked us (the forum at large) to tone things down in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T16:13:01-07:00","id":1542341,"title":"","content":"I like the Predator types myself as it does flesh out on how you think your kindred hunts. IE my Malkavian likes to avoid unneeded suffering and the Sandman type would fit him like a glove compared to the others and as been mentioned can be modfied to fit the game needs. It's also very helpful if your new to the game setting and this can help flesh out what steps to take creating a begineer vampire player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 09-18-2024, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-17T21:40:03-07:00","id":1542350,"title":"","content":"Predator types are certainly interesting, although I think the way they\u2019re implemented could improve. Attaching so many \u201cpoints\u201d to them muddies things more than help. It is like teasing at being a Character Class without committing to being a Character Class. Which is made worse by the fact we already have Clans for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T13:08:26-07:00","id":1542387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542335#post1542335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter that the predator types have less negative impact on PC XP-value balance in V5 than V20 already has in the BP/XP divide; they introduce even more as written if you add them without modification. V5 could actually claim to have an XP balanced starting spread compared to all previous VtM editions (though VtR 2e beat it to the punch) if not for the predator types. Predator types also aren't an exhaustive unalterable list. While the list is fairly comprehensive, there's nothing stopping the ST and players from modifying them or creating new ones if something else would work better (and not just Rule Zero).<br /> <br /> As for carrots and sticks, I mean things outside of the specific pool of mechanics they offer up. If you take two characters that have to different types, but then the course of the story pushes them in the same direction and then end up with identical sheets... all differences regarding feeding are essentially erased. It's not like they offer exclusive traits or something; even if V5's high XP costs and low XP hand outs makes every extra dot at creation that much more impactful.<br /> <br /> Compared to other Vampire editions, the predator types are just taking what would normally be points to flush out a character to the player's desires, and putting them in a &quot;feeding&quot; bucket. It's extra scaffolding in terms of game design. It's not &quot;necessary&quot; but largely serves its purpose of giving more direction on what's important to think about when assigning values to your character's sheet. In V20, you can informally just ask players to explain how their character normally feeds and see if their sheet really meshes with that, and end up with largely the same outcomes; it's just not as baked in.<br /> <br /> I personally find the &quot;should&quot; statement rather odd given that V5 encourages much fresher vampires than older editions did as the default. If one of V5's goals was to make the default closer to newly embraced vampires instead of vampires with a decade or more of being undead under their belts, it makes less sense for the characters to have settled into feeding strategies so much that they can have such a drastic starting impact.<br /> <br /> Also, frankly, if you're going to try to edition war and write fanboy screeds at people every time V5 gets criticized, people aren't going to care even when you make good points. You're just sabotaging your own credibility to discuss these things reasonably. Even more so since the mods just asked us (the forum at large) to tone things down in this regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theodrim's consideratioms don't seem a screed, honestly, they are and articulated essay on why he thinks PTs are functional as play style enablers, also with some critical considerations attached.<br /> <br /> Something I'd add, is that in the typical Vampire city, with no huge numbers of Kindred, Predator Types are also a social scene of sorts: you meet people wheew you feed, were they other Kindreds, other Supernaturals or the kind of people you aree feeding from, of course.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bWith the emphasis V5 puts, at least in words, on street-level stories and Relationship Maps, I feel Predator Types should be used by players and Storytellers alike as a tool to flesh the city and its NPCs more and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T14:52:50-07:00","id":1542397,"title":"","content":"Predator-Types always felt like a bit of an overreach to put it at character-creation this prominently. These muddled heaps of dots in Skill-specializations, Disciplines, Merits/Backgrounds and Flaws act far too much like a locked-in choice. I think it's entirely dependent on what sort of people you have at the table whether focusing on feeding to this degree is important. Predator-Type only matters if the player in question cares about it. For a player who doesn't care nothing about the more restrictive Predator-types would be interesting but that doesn't equate to them simply having to take a less restrictive version giving them something of equal value compared to the person who really cares. Rather, in my opinion, there are plenty of players who don't want to play VtM with their PCs having locked-in feeding-strategies from the beginning. It's addressing a character-question that is interesting to address but not necessary. Predator-Type makes it a necessary question, though, and now a firm answer and categorization are needed where before this was something you could figure out during play.<br /> <br /> The Predator-Type should accommodate the character-concept and not the other way around. And so I think flexibility and minimalism in how impactful picking a Predator-Type is are preferable. The way Predator-Types are presented, though, (unless (somehow) the character concepts fit the confines of how much is stuffed into these Predator-Type-packages) they end up feeling more like a confining option than something that improves the character-creation-process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-18T16:06:51-07:00","id":1542398,"title":"","content":"Even if you want to keep a decent pile of points attached to predator types, it wouldn't be that hard to do it like V5 already does Skills: have three templates (broad eats almost anything, has a strong preference but is flexible, highly specialized) to build the type to fit your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T13:41:04-07:00","id":1542436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542387#post1542387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I'd add, is that in the typical Vampire city, with no huge numbers of Kindred, Predator Types are also a social scene of sorts: you meet people wheew you feed, were they other Kindreds, other Supernaturals or the kind of people you aree feeding from, of course.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bWith the emphasis V5 puts, at least in words, on street-level stories and Relationship Maps, I feel Predator Types should be used by players and Storytellers alike as a tool to flesh the city and its NPCs more and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;with no huge numbers of Kindred&quot; is doing a lot of heavy lifting there... Predator Types are the exact opposite of encouraging cooperation. You have two &quot;Sandman&quot;-types in the same part of town and they're competitors. You have two &quot;Scene-Queen&quot;-types in the same social circle and they're not fans of each other. That's for sure! That's another reason why Predator-Types should be de-emphasized and things like Clan should matter more.<br /> <br /> As for fleshing out the city and NPCs... Predator-types don't add anything special in that regard. You don't need that category in the character-creation-process to have good contacts and allies for the PCs. As for the Domain-stuff from the V5 Players Guide... That again only matters if you have a player who's heavily invested in having a certain Predator-type. Players who aren't like that may start caring about that once they get to the &quot;managing their Domain&quot;-part of V5 via the V5 Players Guide stuff. But I don't see Predator-type necessarily as something meaningful from the jump during character-creation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T15:45:51-07:00","id":1542438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542387#post1542387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something I'd add, is that in the typical Vampire city, with no huge numbers of Kindred, Predator Types are also a social scene of sorts: you meet people wheew you feed, were they other Kindreds, other Supernaturals or the kind of people you aree feeding from, of course.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bWith the emphasis V5 puts, at least in words, on street-level stories and Relationship Maps, I feel Predator Types should be used by players and Storytellers alike as a tool to flesh the city and its NPCs more and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also bears mention with the changes to V5 metaplot and city politics, the &quot;Rack as social space in addition to Elysium&quot; isn't the default or the expectation. It's more akin to Dark Ages, where every vampire has <i>their</i> feeding ground(s) to do as they will (within reason), and if/where/when those overlap it's either claimed by a coterie, shared between allies, or cause for potential conflict. Vampires may not necessarily share predator types to inhabit the same spaces, and to a certain extent it's more cause for harmonious interaction if they <i>don't</i> since they're not necessarily feeding on the same herd.<br /> <br /> Case in point, that Toreador trapdoor I mentioned in the chronicle I'm running. She's in a coterie with a scene queen Tremere and a siren Gangrel. Their shared feeding ground is the local university, where the Tremere has her fingers in sex-positive campus groups and non-profs, and claims a &quot;content&quot; house with a protest group front as her domain. The Tremere's into new agey free love bullshit and has the influence to keep things moving, the Toreador handles the money and does &quot;content&quot;, and the Gangrel gets free &quot;meals&quot; while keeping things safe and consensual (i.e. she's the muscle). They don't feed on the same mortals, but there's enough cross-pollination between their respective herds -- not to mention synergies in their influences -- they accomplish more working together than individually.<br /> <br /> But, onto nitty-gritty...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542397#post1542397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...These muddled heaps of dots in Skill-specializations, Disciplines, Merits/Backgrounds and Flaws act far too much like a locked-in choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of that framework exists to justify how the character feeds (and how feeding preferences would influence dot allocation in the backstory phase), while providing a baseline ability to feed in the first place. The quiet part out loud here is predator type doesn't just influence disciplines, advantages, and flaws -- players still have to allocate attributes and skills before predator type, and once they've put everything together they need a respectable dice pool in their feeding roll of choice, and in the case of some predator types and clans a discipline dot to supplement feeding strategy.<br /> <br /> That's all there to ensure players don't feel they <i>must </i>optimize for feeding, and are freer to allocate dots elsewhere as appropriate to the character. If, for example, a player wanted to run with an alleycat Tremere, it's a pathway to the dot of Celerity or Potence they'd need, as well as contacts or a relevant specialty that might otherwise have to be bought, to justify the feeding strategy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's entirely dependent on what sort of people you have at the table whether focusing on feeding to this degree is important. Predator-Type only matters if the player in question cares about it. For a player who doesn't care nothing about the more restrictive Predator-types would be interesting but that doesn't equate to them simply having to take a less restrictive version giving them something of equal value compared to the person who really cares... </div> </div> </div>See earlier commentary about experienced players and the difficulties of running feeding scenes with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rather, in my opinion, there are plenty of players who don't want to play VtM with their PCs having locked-in feeding-strategies from the beginning. It's addressing a character-question that is interesting to address but not necessary. Predator-Type makes it a necessary question, though, and now a firm answer and categorization are needed where before this was something you could figure out during play. </div> </div> </div>Except, with only a handful of predator types are characters <i>mandated</i> to feed a certain way. There's nothing to stop a siren from starting with (or gaining) fame/influence and feeding scene queen or osiris-style, or just having good combat dice pools enabling alleycat or pursuer-style feeding. A Gangrel or Nosferatu trapdoor can still build up or start with Animalism, and supplement trapdoor feeding with farming when the mortals just aren't around. Graverobbers might be obvious predators, but that flaw only applies when attempting to feed through social wiles -- they can still bag it, or go alleycat or sandman.<br /> <br /> A case in point is a snippet of a scene from that same chronicle, when the PC's were at a party being held by the aforementioned NPC coterie. The Brujah PC was a little peckish, and his player asked to hunt at the party. I said yeah, but since it's a college party he can't exactly beat the piss out of someone, start a fight, or extort them for blood, and the easiest or most obvious way would be to seduce a mortal. He consulted his dice pools for siren-style feeding, realized his character <i>sucked</i> at it, and pointed out something I hadn't considered: it's a college party, there are going to be people passed out drunk or high off their tits, he could sandman it.<br /> <br /> I was more than happy to oblige, and after the disclaimer it may result in his character getting drunk or high, he was able to feed just fine despite having a predator type not at all suited to college parties. Worked out <i>better</i> for him in the short term, since the difficulty bonus against frenzy from weed came in handy a scene later when he had to resist it.<br /> <br /> None of this &quot;locks in&quot; anything, it just establishes a <i>baseline</i> to justify how your character doesn't just starve into torpor or wassail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-19-2024, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T18:13:48-07:00","id":1542441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542438#post1542438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of that framework exists to justify how the character feeds (and how feeding preferences would influence dot allocation in the backstory phase), while providing a baseline ability to feed in the first place. The quiet part out loud here is predator type doesn't just influence disciplines, advantages, and flaws -- players still have to allocate attributes and skills before predator type, and once they've put everything together they need a respectable dice pool in their feeding roll of choice, and in the case of some predator types and clans a discipline dot to supplement feeding strategy.<br /> <br /> That's all there to ensure players don't feel they <i>must </i>optimize for feeding, and are freer to allocate dots elsewhere as appropriate to the character. If, for example, a player wanted to run with an alleycat Tremere, it's a pathway to the dot of Celerity or Potence they'd need, as well as contacts or a relevant specialty that might otherwise have to be bought, to justify the feeding strategy.</div> </div> </div> </div>In trying to argue how Predator Types are not &quot;locked in&quot;, you're just explaining my own point again: These Predator Types only matter if the player in question cares about it. When they don't, they just look at their assortment of dots on the character-sheet and do whatever makes sense for them and the PC at the time when it comes to feeding. So the categorization of Predator Type at character-creation was meaningless in those cases. That character in question isn't really an &quot;Alleycat&quot; or a &quot;Sandman&quot;. The categorization-exercise was meaningless therefore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542438#post1542438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, with only a handful of predator types are characters <i>mandated</i> to feed a certain way. There's nothing to stop a siren from starting with (or gaining) fame/influence and feeding scene queen or osiris-style, or just having good combat dice pools enabling alleycat or pursuer-style feeding. A Gangrel or Nosferatu trapdoor can still build up or start with Animalism, and supplement trapdoor feeding with farming when the mortals just aren't around. Graverobbers might be obvious predators, but that flaw only applies when attempting to feed through social wiles -- they can still bag it, or go alleycat or sandman.<br /> <br /> A case in point is a snippet of a scene from that same chronicle, when the PC's were at a party being held by the aforementioned NPC coterie. The Brujah PC was a little peckish, and his player asked to hunt at the party. I said yeah, but since it's a college party he can't exactly beat the piss out of someone, start a fight, or extort them for blood, and the easiest or most obvious way would be to seduce a mortal. He consulted his dice pools for siren-style feeding, realized his character <i>sucked</i> at it, and pointed out something I hadn't considered: it's a college party, there are going to be people passed out drunk or high off their tits, he could sandman it.<br /> <br /> I was more than happy to oblige, and after the disclaimer it may result in his character getting drunk or high, he was able to feed just fine despite having a predator type not at all suited to college parties. Worked out <i>better</i> for him in the short term, since the difficulty bonus against frenzy from weed came in handy a scene later when he had to resist it.<br /> <br /> None of this &quot;locks in&quot; anything, it just establishes a <i>baseline</i> to justify how your character doesn't just starve into torpor or wassail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the actual baseline: You're a vampire, you drink human blood. Nuff said. There's your <i>real baseline</i>. And your example is a good showcase for why Predator Types are about &quot;locking in&quot; certain choices. If the PC in question just does &quot;whatever feels right/effective&quot; in a scene, they don't have a Predator Type. The ability to do that isn't conveyed by the step of character-creation where you pick your Predator Type.<br /> <br /> So your argumentation just amounts to &quot;Actually, in most cases the Predator Type is irrelevant.&quot;. And that just means in those cases the character-creation step of having a Predator Type was a waste of time. Just give the XP-equivalent of those dots to players and let them figure it out. You would get the same result. It's not like a player knows from the very beginning what sort of situations they will be thrown into anyway. And your example is a good showcase of how the ST won't necessarily accommodate every player's Predator Type in every scene.<br /> <br /> That's why I said before that what the Predator Type step needs is flexibility and minimalism. There's way too much stuff attached to the Predator Type. It's either something a player deeply cares about or will be tossed aside at the earliest moment of inconvenience. Either way, it wasn't the Predator Type step that led to this and was entirely dependent on player-preferences. Does it do anything at all at the end of the day? A player who really cares will restrict themselves to their Predator Type even when it's not one of the heavyweights with feeding-restrictions. A player who doesn't just sees a couple of dots on a page and does whatever feels right. In the case of the latter, the Predator Type categorization overreached and tried to &quot;lock in&quot; a choice the player wasn't interested in - and therefore the player ignores that choice after character-creation. In the case of the former, you just have an accidental alignment between a particular player's character-concept and V5's Predator Type categorization. That concept was there even without the Predator-Type package. So you have one scenario where Predator Type gets ignored and another where the player was already locking in on a particular Predator Type without prompting.<br /> <br /> And then there's of course those Predator Types, as you say, do &quot;mandate to feed in a certain way&quot;. The ones you didn't want to talk about. You know, just those Predator Types that prove how you're dead wrong on the &quot;locked in&quot; part, like a Blood Leech, for example. And those feeding-restrictions are just sitting there alongside those other Predator Types. A bad choice in presentation, I think.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T13:04:35-07:00","id":1542467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542232#post1542232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem in 5th is touchstones are misused as a railroading device rather than a roleplay tool. You're effectively forced to write npcs your pc 'cares' about and they're explicitly muggles since the writters think that makes it more grounded. One of the few times i flipped the figurative table with a game was when a gm nagged me over the entire of session 0 into having a human bff just to make it pregnant with a super wyrm antichrist and i was expected to go through lots of angst and conflict for it. He was upset when i just killed the npc and burnt the feutus because i was playing a shadow lord and just spent an ic weekend mourning her.<br /> <br /> Touchstones feel a lot like that. A lot of potential lousy execution</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be a common mistake a lot of GMs make. They love to make any characters connected to a PC as potential hostages or victims of their antagonists. They think it will make players more involved in their campaign plots. However, this only annoy players because this NPC they supposedly care about is hijacking the game and diverting them from the things they are actually interested in. So not only to players resent it, they tend to do things IC and OOC to eliminate the problem which is to entirely ditch anyone they care about. So instead of a richer setting and supporting cast for the PC - which is often the intent of such characters, it just results in even less setting detail and no supporting cast.<br /> <br /> In a drama, it makes a good scene for Hector Salamanca to put the squeeze on Ignacio Varga's dad because it creates a lot of tension and provides for character building. In a roleplaying game, all it usually does is make the player of Nacho not have a father (or any family or friends) at all and eliminate any kind of roleplay opportunities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5zSxT74WWrc\" data-code=\"5zSxT74WWrc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5zSxT74WWrc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> So as ST, I go out of my way to not have such characters become important to the chronicle so they can remain exclusively part of the player's roleplay, and avoid NPCs targeting them in any fashion. It doesn't always make sense from an IC perspective, but if you want to encourage good roleplay and a supporting cast, it's what needs to be done. So NPCs just ignore the supporting cast of PCs UNLESS the players themselves decide to utilize them in some sort of scheme against the NPCs. That makes them fair game, and players recognize it was them who put their supporting cast member (whether they are just NPCs they interact with or actual Backgrounds/Merits that are on the character sheet) in jeopardy.<br /> <br /> So in the RPG campaign of Better Call Saul, Hector Salamanca never asks Nacho to have his dad's business become a front. Instead, the GM can only have Hector comment he needs one and see if the player of Nacho bites and offers his dad's business. If he does, he then finds out his dad never agrees and threaten to go to the cops. Because the player created the situation, he cares about the dad instead of being angry at the GM for screwing him over.<br /> <br /> Having that guideline has improved my games a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T13:17:11-07:00","id":1542468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542350#post1542350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator types are certainly interesting, although I think the way they\u2019re implemented could improve. Attaching so many \u201cpoints\u201d to them muddies things more than help. It is like teasing at being a Character Class without committing to being a Character Class. Which is made worse by the fact we already have Clans for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Predator types and similar mechanics like Backgrounds in D&amp;D 5e have the same benefits and drawbacks. The benefits are that they provide the means to further customize the character. And in certain ways they prompt the player to think more carefully of their character's backstory. The drawback is that there are only a certain number of them and thus can be overly restrictive and not accommodate certain backstories, and the desire to provide specific benefits for each one can lead to certain features be too good or bad from a mechanics perspective.<br /> <br /> I usually prefer some sort of method of defining some quick and easy way to allow PCs further customization and build points, but not in ways that break the game. So I let the player describe whatever it is they want (My vampires often feeds on the homeless, or my fighter grew up on a farm and worked as a pigkeeper) and collaborate with them on specific benefits. For Vampire that might be the first dot in some Discipline they haven't put points in and the first dot in some Ability. For D&amp;D 5e, that can be two skills they gain proficiency in, a proficiency in either a tool or vehicle, and some extra cash and gear worth a certain amount. That allows for extra customization, but all players get the same benefits. I just use the existing types, backgrounds, careers, whatever they call it in the game, as examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T14:28:00-07:00","id":1542469,"title":"","content":"Predator Types seems like something that should have just been a role-playing aid. Where the character creation chapter would digress into a text box that describes different ways vampires often feed, and why they'd want to. With a list at the bottom of each entry, suggesting Abilities that complement that style.<br /> <br /> It wouldn't be a mechanical system. It could easily be ignored. But it would provide guidance for players who need help deciding on starting dot allocation, or to immerse them in their role as a blood-sucking undead parasite in the modern day.<br /> <br /> (A not-too-dissimilar effect happens in D&amp;D 5e, where each class write-up includes a &quot;Quick Start Guide&quot; telling the player what choices to make if they just want to skip straight to running their Class &quot;Vanilla&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T15:02:39-07:00","id":1542470,"title":"","content":"Fun stuff first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542467#post1542467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ..That seems to be a common mistake a lot of GMs make. They love to make any characters connected to a PC as potential hostages or victims of their antagonists...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that stems from lack of experience and imagination as to what touchstones are and the purposes they could really serve in a chronicle. There's a <i>lot</i> of narrative room to explore the panoply of &quot;vampire&quot; themes there, for players and ST's willing to do the legwork.<br /> <br /> For example, this chronicle I keep mentioning: the elder (mortal age-wide, anyhow) PC is an Hecata. His touchstones are his mortal daughter and grandkids. So naturally, I'm twisting the <i>fuck</i> out of that knife.<br /> <br /> He has the Archaic flaw? His mortal daughter bought him one of those cell phones designed for older folks, because thanks to his &quot;age&quot; and changed habits she thinks he's developing early onset dementia. Fucking fantastic out-of-character comedy beat for the group and it was a nice spot of roleplay since his character had to fake gratitude while being annoyed at the low-key patronization...and it gives his character <i>basic</i> means to communicate since I ruled despite his flaw, the phone's programming is simple enough he can use it -- he just can't use apps or the browser, and can only text with difficulty (not that he wants to), and it annoys the crap out of him he &quot;has&quot; to use it.<br /> <br /> <i>And</i> she's putting subtle pressure on him to retire, maybe even let her set him up in a nice &quot;retirement community&quot;. She has the money to float it with her new job...that was totally a nepotism hire by a Milliner in the city, who did a background check on the PC and found out about the mortal connections. <i>And</i> his granddaughter even got a nice scholarship for AP classes while finishing high school! Family looks out for family, right?<br /> <br /> Frankly, his touchstones are about the best-protected in the entire city thanks to his association. They literally have an entire coterie of ancillae Hecata, and their combined assets, that'll go to the mats to keep them safe. At least as long as the PC remembers his familial responsibilities. Part of which includes that his granddaughter's been &quot;pre-approved&quot; for a set-up with a young Milliner of about the same age. And hey, if that attachment works out she just might be a good candidate for the Proxy Kiss...<br /> <br /> But for now, spontaneous (and frankly, hilarious) absolute shitshows like his daughter needing a last-minute babysitter for a hot date, right in the middle of a citywide political crisis, are absolutely on the table. But I'm a sucker for situational comedy like a <i>vampire</i> having to drag his mortal grandkids around the city (or sneak out after he's put them to bed) as he has to help put out fires.<br /> <br /> Anyhow...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542441#post1542441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In trying to argue how Predator Types are not &quot;locked in&quot;, you're just explaining my own point again...</div> </div> </div> </div>Your last post, the one to which I replied,<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542397#post1542397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...These muddled heaps of dots in Skill-specializations, Disciplines, Merits/Backgrounds and Flaws act far too much like a locked-in choice...players who don't want to play VtM with their PCs having locked-in feeding-strategies...they end up feeling more like a confining option than something that improves the character-creation-process.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quite obviously arguing that is the case. You're only just now changing tact and arguing they're meaningless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...These Predator Types only matter if the player in question cares about it.... </div> </div> </div>As you rightly pointed out, this is a game about blood-drinking predators...and the lengths to which they will go to get their fix, survive, and thrive, and the personal and societal cost thereof. Frankly, I'd suggest that if players aren't interested in, or unwilling to engage with, the core theme of the game and its setting, a storyteller or player looks at how they're presenting/internalizing the material to see what they might do to make that core theme more interesting...and failing that, conclude this game <i>may</i> not be the one for them.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't use D&amp;D -- an adaption of a tabletop war game with bare bones and inadequate social mechanics -- to run a Martin-esque political dark fantasy, or even a Tolkien-esque high fantasy with strongly philosophical and naturalist themes. That's fundamentally in conflict with what D&amp;D is, and what type of play it best-fits.<br /> <br /> That's a far cry from experienced players who are just bored with feeding scenes, the scenario I discussed. As, even though they get bored with feeding scenes, they still understand what this game is and its full implications, and as consequence consider how their characters feed as a core part of that character identity. It's precisely <i>because of</i> that fluency they get bored with feeding scenes, because they simply never needed it to reinforce theme or setting.<br /> <br /> That's a group with which I <i>only</i> ever played Revised and V20, because to be frank, I wasn't about to get them up to speed on a new edition without damned good reason, and we split up during Covid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...When they don't, they just look at their assortment of dots on the character-sheet and do whatever makes sense for them and the PC at the time when it comes to feeding... </div> </div> </div>That's...kind of the idea. Vampires are creatures of habit, and predator type is loosely understood to be how a character is accustomed to feeding when nothing else is going on -- either during backstory or downtime. Necessity, like the sort of necessity that happens during a story, just happens to breed innovation, even among vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...So your argumentation just amounts to &quot;Actually, in most cases the Predator Type is irrelevant&quot;... </div> </div> </div>No, and no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...It's not like a player knows from the very beginning what sort of situations they will be thrown into anyway... </div> </div> </div>This is why we have session zero's, and conversations with players about their characters during the generation phase of play. Would this be a debate if we were discussing a thread in which a ST bemoaned that a player brought a combat monster Brujah to a low-combat, high-social, political chronicle? or a Malkavian without combat skills to a high-octane action chronicle? or a dipshit Gangrel to a chronicle all about hunting for and discovering occult secrets?<br /> <br /> No, of course not. We'd all be saying, &quot;why didn't you tell your player what the chronicle was going to be about, silly? You brought this situation on yourself by inadequately communicating with your players.&quot; Why is this scenario any different just because it happens to involve a V5-specific mechanic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...And your example is a good showcase of how the ST won't necessarily accommodate every player's Predator Type in every scene.... </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and it's <i>also</i> an example of how my player and I worked together to accommodate feeding apart from predator type, but still in-character. Frankly, no kidding not every predator type can possibly be accommodated in every scene in which a character might want to feed. That's an impossibly high standard, and frankly, one that not even previous editions could uphold.<br /> <br /> I mean, are predator types &quot;locked-in&quot; choices or are they not? You're talking at cross purposes, here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...It's either something a player deeply cares about or will be tossed aside at the earliest moment of inconvenience... </div> </div> </div>This is why we have predator types with different levels of restriction. They're available for players who feel a certain aspect of feeding is key to their character, but players aren't obligated to take them. Again, what do we expect here?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...And then there's of course those Predator Types, as you say, do &quot;mandate to feed in a certain way&quot;. The ones you didn't want to talk about... </div> </div> </div>When I was the one to voluntarily present a fairly-comprehensive list of those predator types, and have been discussing the role of those types in character generation -- and the mechanical and narrative implications of selecting one -- I fail to see how I might be described as not wanting to talk about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T09:25:01-07:00","id":1542483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542467#post1542467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to be a common mistake a lot of GMs make. They love to make any characters connected to a PC as potential hostages or victims of their antagonists. They think it will make players more involved in their campaign plots. However, this only annoy players because this NPC they supposedly care about is hijacking the game and diverting them from the things they are actually interested in. So not only to players resent it, they tend to do things IC and OOC to eliminate the problem which is to entirely ditch anyone they care about. So instead of a richer setting and supporting cast for the PC - which is often the intent of such characters, it just results in even less setting detail and no supporting cast.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah this is one of the reasons the cliche of 'loner' in common in wod-nobody wants to waste their evening messing around with grandma getting abducted by the sabbat for the 3rd time and frankly a lot players don't really want to spend their gaming time interacting with fake-mum (I spend enough time avoiding my real one lol), I generally tend to consider friends and family off limits unless there's an in game mechanic attached to them. trouble is with touchstones is punitive making them more of a lead weight than anything, largely because it's there to force the player to engage in way the game wants. This is why I implemented them as a beneficial background because this requires the player to opt in and makes it worth it, it also makes it more acceptable for me to mess with them like I would any resource a kindred has-killing retainers, wrecking your business, forcing you to cash in boons etc.<br /> <br /> You can't make me care I can only choose to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T12:49:02-07:00","id":1542493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542468#post1542468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Predator types and similar mechanics like Backgrounds in D&amp;D 5e have the same benefits and drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and I work in a very similar way. In this regard, I think Backgrounds are a lot better as a mechanic precisely because they define far simpler aspects of the character sheet, so it is an important step, but not something that overtakes the character creation, and are also easier to make or change.<br /> <br /> As a V20 mechanic, it could be one extra Ability dot and two Specializations. It\u2019s interesting to have a source of Specializations that isn\u2019t being a pro with 4+ dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542470#post1542470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you rightly pointed out, this is a game about blood-drinking predators...and the lengths to which they will go to get their fix, survive, and thrive, and the personal and societal cost thereof. Frankly, I'd suggest that if players aren't interested in, or unwilling to engage with, the core theme of the game and its setting, a storyteller or player looks at how they're presenting/internalizing the material to see what they might do to make that core theme more interesting...and failing that, conclude this game <i>may</i> not be the one for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has nothing to do with the central problem of Predator Types making too much of a starting character sheet.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re so obsessed with defending V5 from any perceived slight that you can\u2019t simply accept that people just as experienced as you at STing, and that actually like the mechanic\u2019s general idea, would prefer to reduce the amount of dots \u201clocked\u201d in it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, you\u2019re edition warrying <b>again</b> for nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T23:49:02-07:00","id":1542507,"title":"","content":"Im actually kind of curious about this <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> how often do you run feeding scenes on average?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-22T15:10:04-07:00","id":1542516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542507#post1542507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im actually kind of curious about this <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar431_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"431\" data-vbnamecard=\"431\">Theodrim</a> how often do you run feeding scenes on average?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's too open-ended a question to answer in any meaningful way, because it's not going to give answers with any value.<br /> <br /> It's not about &quot;averages&quot;, it's about who's at the table, what their interests are, how experienced they are with the setting and game system, their skill as role-players, what themes I'm looking to explore in a given chronicle, how developed a chronicle is versus my planned length for it, what I have planned for that session versus the &quot;open play&quot; time I've slotted into it, whether players have taken interest in the establishment for a given scene, the amount of &quot;screen time&quot; each player may get as a consequence as a solo versus group feeding scenes (as a matter of fairness and maintaining player interest), and a healthy dose of what &quot;feels right&quot; in the moment. And likewise, the amount of time I <i>spend</i> on feeding scenes -- whether it's fully role-played out, or it's a &quot;narrate and go with a die roll&quot; resolution -- depends heavily on all of the above factors.<br /> <br /> It's better if I give what I consider to be some &quot;ground rules&quot; for how I run feeding scenes. Regardless of group, I at least try to do them at least once per story especially if it's a newer chronicle and players need time to discover their characters, if we skipped a game session (or had a short hiatus) and players need a bit of a warm-up, if players start losing sight of playing vampires, or if I think it'll shake things up a bit narratively.<br /> <br /> Regardless of systems, hunger mechanics (V5 hunger dice or past editions' blood points, it doesn't matter) are a nice mediating influence by coincidence. At least the way I run, if one or more characters <i>need</i> to feed, it's usually a consequence of a particularly intense scene, or number of scenes in which I've been applying narrative pressure that precludes feeding. After which, players may need or highly value a breather, or bit of catharsis, by way of feeding scenes. Or to put it another way, if characters are a mite peckish after a fight with elders or werewolves in which they could well have died, it feels nice to bully some mortals and reassert a sense of agency or even dominance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-22-2024, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T01:47:45-07:00","id":1542525,"title":"","content":"Yeah this matches most peoples general mindset , including my own of the game (although imo the actual horror of vtm comes from the things you dont <i>have </i>to do and how it all eventually becomes routine) so im unclear what your arguement is in defence off?<br /> <br /> The predator system is imo bloat it isnt very useful outside of schaffolding and more commonly some people think its overemphasised on the sheet even if they like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-23-2024, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T16:03:36-07:00","id":1542536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542525#post1542525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah this matches most peoples general mindset , including my own of the game (although imo the actual horror of vtm comes from the things you dont <i>have </i>to do and how it all eventually becomes routine) so im unclear what your arguement is in defence off?<br /> <br /> The predator system is imo bloat it isnt very useful outside of schaffolding and more commonly some people think its overemphasised on the sheet even if they like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not entirely sure what more you expect me to say, here. I already addressed the point on the first and second pages of this thread; to wit, my very post in it was specifically about this issue. At the end of the day this is still a tabletop role-playing game about undead blood-drinking predators. Yes, how characters get their fix should be an integral part of that experience, from the point of character generation on because a player will have to justify how their character feeds.<br /> <br /> What predator type does, is formalize that process by providing baseline dots with in-built functionality relevant to that player's choice of how their character feeds.<br /> <br /> I pointed out before, players being bored with or desensitized to feeding scenes does not equate to players being disinterested in or disengaged with the game's core theme. These are two issues separate and distinct from each other, with their own root causes and pathways to resolution for the sake of a better overall experience for everyone at the table.<br /> <br /> My veteran group with whom I didn't run feeding scenes, didn't need them <i>because they had so thoroughly internalized that core theme it no longer needed reinforcement</i>. That doesn't mean they didn't care how their characters fed, or paid no attention to it when declaring their characters on the hunt; rather, they volunteered necessary or relevant information on declaration because they knew if they didn't, I was going to pick up the slack. Whatever degree of shorthand that followed, was subordinate to our mutual understanding of the game and each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T23:06:17-07:00","id":1542541,"title":"","content":"And my counter point is that its unessicary bloat, if i remove the predator types from v5 and instead just ask the player to roll the relavent skill set its actually a lot more intuative with the game and how the pc feeds and v5s stripped down back to basics mindset.<br /> <br /> Edit as a tangent its quite interesting that your gaming approach to feeding is effectively the same as someone who doesnt find it as critical to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-24-2024, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T09:52:17-07:00","id":1542557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542541#post1542541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my counter point is that its unessicary bloat, if i remove the predator types from v5 and instead just ask the player to roll the relavent skill set its actually a lot more intuative with the game and how the pc feeds and v5s stripped down back to basics mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, is it?<br /> <br /> I could break down V5 versus previous edition character generation step-by-step, but in the end V5 has one fewer step overall by way of rolling backgrounds, merits, and flaws together, and replacing freebie points with predator type. Freebie points were by far the most problematic step of previous edition character generation -- freebie point-buys had wildly divergent experience cost discrepancies, were the biggest decision paralysis invoker and stumbling block for newer and less rules-fluent players. The difference between an experienced player's, and a newbie's, starting characters could be massive to the point of disrupting game balance for easily the first hundred experience points' worth of play.<br /> <br /> That's without going into the storyteller headache resultant from potential merit/flaw munchkinism, having to audit at char gen to make sure someone didn't accidentally spend too many or too few freebies, and checking for odd, inappropriate, or hard-to-justify freebie expenditure. That's without assuming negative player intent -- sometimes a player just gets overexcited, loses focus during character generation, suffers from decision paralysis, or slips into old habit. I do it too -- a recent V20 character I made was a Nosferatu ancilla recently out of a long torpor, and I as someone who likes to play characters with the drive skill, had to consciously remind myself this is not a character on whom points in drive would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Can you justifiably call something unnecessary bloat, when it overall reduces the number of steps to character generation and directly replaces a far more problematic step? Commentary thus far is just restricted to character generation.<br /> <br /> In play, predator type recommends predetermined dice pools for feeding. That's one fewer decision point for a storyteller to make, while establishing a player expectation of how they might be able to approach a circumstance outside character specialty or expertise. It amounts to less time and mental bandwidth to be spent on game mechanics over the course of a session, story, or chronicle, which can then be spent on story and narration -- the things that really matter in a narrative-focused game. And most importantly, it reduces the potential for squabbling over which dice pool might be most appropriate for a given situation by keeping everyone on the same page.<br /> <br /> Is it perfect? no. But &quot;imperfect&quot; is not synonymous with &quot;bad&quot;, least of all when the systems replaced are even more problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T10:40:21-07:00","id":1542559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542470#post1542470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you misunderstand. My point is that the point of a Predator Type is that the PC in question is using one (!) strategy to feed - and ONLY one. And if you're not doing that - the Predator Type step is meaningless. If the PC is in a scene, the player decides they want to feed, the ST describes the scene, the PC decides on how they're going to feed depending on the present circumstances and whatever feels right at that moment... That character does NOT have a Predator Type.<br /> <br /> And what you seem to not understand is: That's what you do. Your game doesn't have Predator Types. The main-purpose of a Predator Type is to present a &quot;feeding-restriction&quot;. Whereas the more advanced ones like Blood-Leech have hard-coded this in terms of Flaws, even a Sandman or a Siren Queen are defined by having a very particular routine. There's no spontaneity to how a vampire feeds in V5. Predator Types create a predetermined preference that PCs are supposed to rarely deviate from.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how V5 defines Predator Types.<br /> <br /> Aside from the big heap of various dots and things that are attached to it, official books give you a description like: &quot;How a Kindred hunts their prey defines their unlife, more than perhaps any other aspect of their nature. Your chosen (or obsessive) hunting pattern arguably affects you even more than your clan does.&quot; (V5 Players Guide pg. 106). And ranging from how the Domain-rules in the V5 Players Guide encourage players to tie what territories your Coterie controls to what their respective Predator Types are to the book Crimosn Gutter having a whole chapter in Crimosn Gutter about Complications on the hunt tied to Predator Types and a table for the selected list of a couple of activities particular Predator Types engage in... The idea is that your Predator Type is the one hunting/feeding strategy PCs rely on. Whenever it's not that, it's an emergency, not just a spontaneous change of pace.<br /> <br /> And my point is... if you don't do that, then Predator Types are meaningless. There's absolutely no reason to attach this much stuff to this if you don't play it like that.\u200b<br /> <br /> Of course, that then brings us back to the &quot;locked in&quot;-question and you deviating from the official conception of Predator Types at your table just shows the flaws of the idea. Could a more freeform way lead to problems? Sure. And so can trying to have to accommodate that one PC with the Consensualist Predator Type. In a way, Predator Types solve nothing and just create different problems. It's a very different approach, though, that presumes the players are deciding on this restriction during character-creation. If you're not running with the idea of characters having their one hunting/feeding-strategy they're obsessed with, then Predator Type as a character-creation-step is too big in its impact on character-creation.<br /> <br /> The point of V5's Predator Types is that PCs are supposed to stick to them. And if they don't, that's bad. When you're not doing that, you're not in a game with Predator Types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:47:56-07:00","id":1542564,"title":"","content":"V5: Can we have Auspices?<br /> <br /> V5 Direction: We have Auspices at home.<br /> <br /> (Cue V5 looking at Predator types)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:49:56-07:00","id":1542565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542559#post1542559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least, that's how V5 defines Predator Types.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it expressly is not. V5 corebook, page 175, emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1664_1727201916237_812\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1664\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1664\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1664&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...Your hunting <b>preferences</b> feed your Blood, and your Blood shapes what Skills and even Disciplines you develop as a vampire. This modus predationis is how you <b>usually</b> hunt. Your Predator type shows <b>your reflex or habit</b>; it <b>doesn\u2019t mandate your behavior in the game</b>. You <b>can hunt in other fashions during a game session</b>, since you may need to cooperate with other Predator types and <b>take advantage of feeding opportunities that appear during the story</b>... </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's supposed to be a preference and habituated activity. Vampires in popular culture and folklore have always been depicted as heavily habitual, to borderline/outright compulsive. It's <i>not</i> a mandate, with the exception of very few, <i>optional</i>, predator types with specific restrictions. You are criticizing the mechanic on the basis of incorrect assumptions. And using those assumptions to say that if predator type is restrictive, it's <i>too</i> restrictive and predeterminant on a character while enforcing specific styles on players who may not necessarily want to engage with the game on that level, but if it's not restrictive it's meaningless. This is a falsely dichotomous, &quot;damned if you do and damned if you don't&quot; position. So, which is it?<br /> <br /> The reason I reply here, is because if you're going to justifiably criticize V5 mechanics -- or for the purposes of this thread, export mechanics to a previous edition -- you need to get them right first, as opposed to build straw men. Like taking my example of how I worked with a player to accommodate their character's need to feed as indicative I don't play to predator type <i>at all</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:35:15-07:00","id":1542575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542565#post1542565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it expressly is not. V5 corebook, page 175, emphasis mine.<br /> Yes, it's supposed to be a preference and habituated activity. Vampires in popular culture and folklore have always been depicted as heavily habitual, to borderline/outright compulsive. It's <i>not</i> a mandate, with the exception of very few, <i>optional</i>, predator types with specific restrictions. You are criticizing the mechanic on the basis of incorrect assumptions. And using those assumptions to say that if predator type is restrictive, it's <i>too</i> restrictive and predeterminant on a character while enforcing specific styles on players who may not necessarily want to engage with the game on that level, but if it's not restrictive it's meaningless. This is a falsely dichotomous, &quot;damned if you do and damned if you don't&quot; position. So, which is it?<br /> <br /> The reason I reply here, is because if you're going to justifiably criticize V5 mechanics -- or for the purposes of this thread, export mechanics to a previous edition -- you need to get them right first, as opposed to build straw men. Like taking my example of how I worked with a player to accommodate their character's need to feed as indicative I don't play to predator type <i>at all</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you call an &quot;incorrect assumption&quot; is <i>a quote from an official V5 book</i>... I was trying to show you how it's presented in the books. Especially in the supplements. I know what it says in the corebook. But the official game hasn't been following up on your definition of what Predator Types are but rather with what I've outlined. If your argument is &quot;As far as V5 is concerned, I only care about the corebook.&quot;, sure okay. So your position on the V5 mechanic is to selectively ignore all the books that have been released after the corebook. If that's the position you wanna go with, sure.<br /> <br /> And you still don't understand what I'm getting at: If you don't play Predator Types like how I explained before, you don't need it to be this special step during character-creation. Previous editions didn't have this because if feeding-strategies are an amalgamation of character-concept, dots on the char-sheet and whatever feels right at the moment anyway, the V5-Predator-Type as a character-creation-step becomes irrelevant. You don't need this step if Predator Type isn't about locking things down in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Also, in terms of character-creation your presentation makes little sense. What you're advocating for is a PC who's a Sandman who never does Sandman-stuff for their feeding-strategy makes sense in V5. What you seem to be confused about is that you have yet to make a good case for why you think the Predator-Type-character-creation-step is needed. Your presentation of Predator-Type talks a lot about how it's not about &quot;locking in&quot; but you present no affirmative case for why the Predator-Type-character needed to be there in the first place.<br /> <br /> And that's also why the V5 supplements emphasized Predator Types in the &quot;locked in&quot; direction and not in the direction of fluidity a la &quot;vampires are switching between Predator Types all the time&quot; or &quot;Predator Type is a preference, nothing more. Actually, it isn't that big of a deal.&quot;. When your character is a Siren Queen, the player shouldn't be like &quot;If I have to beat up a guy in this alley to drink blood, I will beat up a guy in this alley to drink blood.&quot;. To make it meaningful and justify its status as this extra step in character-creation, the surest way to pronounce that meaningfulness is to make Predator Types about &quot;locking in&quot; on a certain hunting-strategy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T13:42:30-07:00","id":1542577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542557#post1542557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except, is it?<br /> <br /> I could break down V5 versus previous edition character generation step-by-step, but in the end V5 has one fewer step overall by way of rolling backgrounds, merits, and flaws together, and replacing freebie points with predator type. Freebie points were by far the most problematic step of previous edition character generation -- freebie point-buys had wildly divergent experience cost discrepancies, were the biggest decision paralysis invoker and stumbling block for newer and less rules-fluent players. The difference between an experienced player's, and a newbie's, starting characters could be massive to the point of disrupting game balance for easily the first hundred experience points' worth of play.<br /> <br /> That's without going into the storyteller headache resultant from potential merit/flaw munchkinism, having to audit at char gen to make sure someone didn't accidentally spend too many or too few freebies, and checking for odd, inappropriate, or hard-to-justify freebie expenditure. That's without assuming negative player intent -- sometimes a player just gets overexcited, loses focus during character generation, suffers from decision paralysis, or slips into old habit. I do it too -- a recent V20 character I made was a Nosferatu ancilla recently out of a long torpor, and I as someone who likes to play characters with the drive skill, had to consciously remind myself this is not a character on whom points in drive would be appropriate.<br /> <br /> Can you justifiably call something unnecessary bloat, when it overall reduces the number of steps to character generation and directly replaces a far more problematic step? Commentary thus far is just restricted to character generation.<br /> <br /> In play, predator type recommends predetermined dice pools for feeding. That's one fewer decision point for a storyteller to make, while establishing a player expectation of how they might be able to approach a circumstance outside character specialty or expertise. It amounts to less time and mental bandwidth to be spent on game mechanics over the course of a session, story, or chronicle, which can then be spent on story and narration -- the things that really matter in a narrative-focused game. And most importantly, it reduces the potential for squabbling over which dice pool might be most appropriate for a given situation by keeping everyone on the same page.<br /> <br /> Is it perfect? no. But &quot;imperfect&quot; is not synonymous with &quot;bad&quot;, least of all when the systems replaced are even more problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once again your framing it in the context of edition comparisons. All you actually need as presented in v5 to replace it is a single dice pool dependant on how you hunt correct?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T14:20:50-07:00","id":1542580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542577#post1542577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again your framing it in the context of edition comparisons. All you actually need as presented in v5 to replace it is a single dice pool dependant on how you hunt correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd made it into an extra Ability dot and one Specialization, maybe two. I do find it useful to have the Predator Type add something, however you interpret it as the habit building skill or the skill building habit.<br /> <br /> On another note, does someone have an idea on how to translate Hunger Dice to V20 or VtR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T15:22:20-07:00","id":1542585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542575#post1542575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you call an &quot;incorrect assumption&quot; is <i>a quote from an official V5 book</i>...</div> </div> </div> </div>What you quoted was explanatory text that predator type has greater impact on a vampire's individual development than clan, roleplay tips and suggestions on how to play to type, and potential complications and narrative hooks as a result of it. None of that can -- or should -- be construed as contradictory to the corebook's text, or taken as assertive of predator type being a mandate on how a character feeds. The corebook's own text still stands; you're reading what you want into that text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't need this step if Predator Type isn't about locking things down in some fashion. </div> </div> </div>You do when the point is to <i>facilitate</i> a chosen hunting and feeding strategy. Predator types with prey restrictions are <i>optional</i>, but permissive predator types still <i>facilitate</i> a chosen feeding strategy. As I stated earlier (which you seem to have missed), the idea is to not force players into feeling they <i>must</i> min-max predator pools, and thereby distribute attribute and ability dots elsewhere they may feel more relevant to the character. And likewise, to <i>facilitate</i> play outside clan stereotype -- the Tremere alleycat, as I suggested earlier.<br /> <br /> That's more than just the consequence of specialties, backgrounds, and merits -- it's also the consequence of <i>disciplines</i> granted by predator type, as well.<br /> <br /> &quot;You <i>must</i> do this one thing&quot; is not an equivalent statement to &quot;you're simply better at this one thing, because you do it as a matter of habit and necessity&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you seem to be confused about is that you have yet to make a good case for why you think the Predator-Type-character-creation-step is needed. Your presentation of Predator-Type talks a lot about how it's not about &quot;locking in&quot; but you present no affirmative case for why the Predator-Type-character needed to be there in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Or, are you just predisposed to reject any argument about it, because your mind is already made up about it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's also why the V5 supplements emphasized Predator Types in the &quot;locked in&quot; direction... </div> </div> </div>Again, that's not what the supplements are actually saying. That's what you've read into it, based on the assumptions you've already made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542577#post1542577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Once again your framing it in the context of edition comparisons. All you actually need as presented in v5 to replace it is a single dice pool dependant on how you hunt correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, it's a thread about exporting V5 mechanics to previous editions (and by extension, the prudence of doing so).<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542580#post1542580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On another note, does someone have an idea on how to translate Hunger Dice to V20 or VtR?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not entirely sure how that would be done elegantly. I wouldn't use Hunger dice per se, but rather rule that if a character is &quot;hungry&quot; (BP equal to or less than seven minus Self-Control, as per V20 rules) dramatic success defaults to messy critical, and failure defaults to bestial failure. Botching in V20 is so rare it's barely worth hinging a mechanic to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T16:34:01-07:00","id":1542592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542585#post1542585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, are you just predisposed to reject any argument about it, because your mind is already made up about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you? Have you already made your mind up? Seems like you're just talking about yourself right there...<br /> <br /> You sound conspiratorially paranoid right there... Might I remind you that you're not a mind-reader and you don't know what my predispositions are... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you quoted was explanatory text that predator type has greater impact on a vampire's individual development than clan, roleplay tips and suggestions on how to play to type, and potential complications and narrative hooks as a result of it. None of that can -- or should -- be construed as contradictory to the corebook's text, or taken as assertive of predator type being a mandate on how a character feeds. The corebook's own text still stands; you're reading what you want into that text. </div> </div> </div>sigh<br /> <br /> You haven't read the supplements I mentioned, have you? Or have ever used the Domain-system from the expanded Coterie-system as outlined in the V5 Players Guide? Have you ever even looked at the way Domain Merits are described...?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, that's not what the supplements are actually saying. That's what you've read into it, based on the assumptions you've already made. </div> </div> </div>Wow, now you're just making baseless claims. I don't think I need to be &quot;predisposed&quot; to reject &quot;I wish this were true.&quot;-arguments like the one you're making here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You must do this one thing&quot; is not an equivalent statement to &quot;you're simply better at this one thing, because you do it as a matter of habit and necessity&quot;. </div> </div> </div>See, that's still lacking... Then why categorize it? If it's just a personal preference for a character, you don't need Predator Types.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T22:23:09-07:00","id":1542608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542585#post1542585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dude, it's a thread about exporting V5 mechanics to previous editions (and by extension, the prudence of doing so).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True but on its own terms its not a great mechanic and thats my point. Hence why i wouldnt import it even in tne context of your arguement even if i agreed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T22:53:05-07:00","id":1542609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542580#post1542580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd made it into an extra Ability dot and one Specialization, maybe two. I do find it useful to have the Predator Type add something, however you interpret it as the habit building skill or the skill building habit.<br /> <br /> On another note, does someone have an idea on how to translate Hunger Dice to V20 or VtR?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i can see that working. Its simple and doesnt clog the game up much. I tend to view it more as a tool for roleplaying than anything and one that isnt needed. Its also why i disgarded clan compulsions and the humor systems immediatly in v5 and the avatar storm in mage.<br /> <br /> The usual advice for hunger dice is simply to make a rouse roll whenever youd spend a blood point which worked okay when i tried it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-25T19:12:04-07:00","id":1542656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542609#post1542609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> i can see that working. Its simple and doesnt clog the game up much. I tend to view it more as a tool for roleplaying than anything and one that isnt needed. Its also why i disgarded clan compulsions and the humor systems immediatly in v5 and the avatar storm in mage.<br /> <br /> The usual advice for hunger dice is simply to make a rouse roll whenever youd spend a blood point which worked okay when i tried it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but which pool to use as rouse rolls?<br /> <br /> Overall the idea of substituting bookkeeping for random chance is pretty interesting to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T09:18:47-07:00","id":1542869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542656#post1542656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, but which pool to use as rouse rolls?<br /> <br /> Overall the idea of substituting bookkeeping for random chance is pretty interesting to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You roll a number of dice equal to the cost in vitae. So 1BP = one die in your rouse check. Because there's a 50% chance of success (ignoring 1s and 10s), having up to 5 Hunger Dice is the same as having 10 BP. If you have more than 10 BP, it gets a bit trickier but if you increase the blood pool by 2 per Generation instead of 1, it works okay again.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, as I suggested when V5 first came out, you can just give Hunger Dice whenever characters fall below 5 blood points, but that makes Hunger much less of an issue. You can tweak it by saying that the first Hunger Die comes as soon as you're at 9 vitae, the second at 7, the third at 5, the fourth at 3, and the fifth at 1. Or even do 9/6/4/2/1 or something.<br /> <br /> Here is a thread on Reddit with some more ideas: <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRPG/comments/izi44f/porting_hunger_dice_into_v20/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/WhiteWolfRP...dice_into_v20/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T11:39:47-07:00","id":1542873,"title":"","content":"About the only thing I'd take from V5 would be the way that Merits are presented as extensions of appropriate Backgrounds; and that's a trivial thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T21:05:07-07:00","id":1542888,"title":"","content":"I like V5's combination of Generation and Blood Potency. VtM has since day one had elder vampires whiling away the ages in torpor and seeing their appetites grow darker over the centuries as storytelling devices, but V5 was the first iteration of the VtM game line to have a mechanic for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T11:46:00-07:00","id":1542969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542888#post1542888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like V5's combination of Generation and Blood Potency. VtM has since day one had elder vampires whiling away the ages in torpor and seeing their appetites grow darker over the centuries as storytelling devices, but V5 was the first iteration of the VtM game line to have a mechanic for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's way too complicated for what it is, though. It needs to be streamlined massively. The BP table shouldn't be much more complicated than the VTR2e one. The problem, I think, is they're trying to make it work with rouse checks instead of blood points\u2014when the latter is far simpler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T13:34:45-07:00","id":1542978,"title":"","content":"I agree, i kinda like the solution for BP of VTR. The whole Hunger dice system should be reworked imho. enough is written on its advantages and disadvantages, we could fill books with it. I just hope we wont gete another &quot;USB&quot; scenario.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T15:08:01-07:00","id":1542982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542969#post1542969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's way too complicated for what it is, though. It needs to be streamlined massively. The BP table shouldn't be much more complicated than the VTR2e one. The problem, I think, is they're trying to make it work with rouse checks instead of blood points\u2014when the latter is far simpler.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally... the complexity undermines the idea of having stronger rules for VtM vampires having darker appetites as they age.<br /> <br /> In pre-V5 the rules (which did exist) where generally hand-wavy and/or optional, but at least could be applied to make it happen to any vampire that clings on long enough.<br /> <br /> By meshing Generation and Blood Potency, V5 results in high Generation vampires that will never inherently get into really morally dubious areas of thirst (a 12 Gen V5 vampire born in the 1000s never goes above BP 3 unless they lower their Gen below 12), where a Gen 4 V5 vampire is created already in pretty dark feeding habits off the bat (min BP of 5). <br /> <br /> I don't entirely agree that rouse checks are at fault here. They don't help, but the bigger problem is that the game decided to express more supernatural power inelegantly: essentially trying to represent older vampires as having larger stores of vitae in four different methods that don't directly scale together. You can simplify the V5 BP chart immensely by having all of the five middle columns (no reason not to toss Bane Severity in this) by having everything be BP/2 round up and then tack on an exception that Superficial Damage healing can be used to heal 1 even at BP 0. I'm not sure most people would notice the difference, and &quot;BP/2 round up&quot; is a lot easier to memorize than a big chart that's close to but not exactly BP/2 sometimes up sometimes down.<br /> <br /> There are other options that keep the idea of a rouse check and not go back to blood points (I'm not personally sold that random is better for this, but lots of people like it so no reason not to have good rules for it), without ditching the idea of older/low Gen vampires being more powerful. As a starting point, you could look at something like advantage/disadvantage in new d20 systems. Weaker vampires have disadvantaged rouse checks, grow into normal rouse checks, and powerful vampires have advantaged rouse checks.. and you'd maintain the larger conceit in a much simpler fashion; though three steps might not be enough to make it feel right. There's also things like how Storypath will sometimes represent characters that are inherently more powerful as having a reduced target number for their rolls. You could modify rouse checks the same way where instead of everyone operating on 50/50, the odds get better towards passing your check and not getting hungry as you go up in power. Either approach means you can keep the impact of rouse checks the same, but skew the math so that stronger vampires fail checks less frequently and thus can do more without getting hungry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T16:41:53-07:00","id":1542986,"title":"","content":"I personally think bringing BP to Masquerade was a bad call. For the setting of VtM I think that it works very well with the idea that low gen vampires start off with a lot of \u201cbrute force\u201d (big pools, big spending, higher limits for buffing with blood), but no refinement (actual dots in Disciplines, Attributes and Abilities).<br /> <br /> For me it would have been better to create a new and simpler table for age, making the effects of becoming an old monster distinct. Bane Severity, Feeding Penalties and Discipline Power Bonus would be transferred from the Generation table to the new Age table.<br /> <br /> Another thing that could be done would be to link some new Discipline powers to age, specially powers that do not require a Rouse Check. I picture transcendence through Discipline as a thing of age, more than Generation, and it would be interesting to give age actual fangs that give Neonates pause whenever they have to face anything really old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T17:34:17-07:00","id":1542988,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how well it fits with VtM broadly, but the one thing about BP that I feel is a cool addition is that torpor reduces BP; or at least can. For vampires seeking power, that's a bad thing, which to vampires seeking a more moral existence that can be a good thing, but broadly it meshes with long standing pop culture vampires &quot;waking up weak&quot; from extended slumber (something that's even in some of the older VtM books on various levels). <br /> <br /> If you just make it age, and cut the reduction in power, you lose a lot of story hooks that add to the game and you don't really gain anything for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T18:10:37-07:00","id":1543043,"title":"","content":"Most of the \u201cvampire awakens weak\u201d tropes I\u2019ve seen are focused on the short term. An ancient vampire needs something between hours and weeks (at the worst) to recover, and more often than not it is just a matter of drinking enough blood (sometimes you need a ritual).<br /> <br /> Overall I think VtR already works well with this idea of diminishing power through the Sleep of Ages, but Masquerade works more on the front that truly ancient vampires are also truly dangerous ones, and often even capable of some level of agency even sleeping. It also works with the idea that the more you age, the more your torpors become long and frequent, while reducing power makes for fresh starts.<br /> <br /> What I don\u2019t think is that this would work only with downsides. Some sort of power must come from age, other than more XP. It may be an increase in Discipline power beyond Generation limits (only a few, but still). It may be a growing capacity to use Disciplines while in Torpor. It may be something akin to Earthbound Merits to increase aspects of existing powers. One way or another, some benefit that can't be acquired through any (or almos any) other means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T09:38:58-07:00","id":1543343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1539998-what-v5-mechanics-would-do-you-port-to-v20?p=1542580#post1542580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, does someone have an idea on how to translate Hunger Dice to V20 or VtR?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not an easy solution, but I ended up making my own VTR spin using V5 dice mechanics, since I like the smaller dice pool and the roughly 50% chances of success per dice, I feel it\u2019s easier to calculate the odds.<br /> <br /> For humanity I made my own table with a static pool and variable difficulties instead of a static difficulty with variable pool like VTR.<br /> <br /> I also remade the VTR discipline using the powers in V5, because I originally liked the idea of different discipline powers, but, after playing with powers for a bit, I realized I like the more structured disciplines of VTR. It took a lot of effort so I would advise against doing that. If I end up running VTR again, I\u2019ll probably just port the VTR disciplines and devotions to my own system.<br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t enjoy reworking systems as much as I do, I\u2019m fairly sure the hunger dices are portable to VTR.<br /> <br /> If I were to port hunger dice to VTR, I\u2019d probably make all discipline cost 1 rouse check per two blood points, up to 3 rouse checks. I\u2019d give rouse check reroll for disciplines dot below BP/2 rounded up.<br /> <br /> As for how to handle hunger dice and messy critical, there are a few interesting ways :<br /> <br /> <b>- As V5 : </b>A pair of 10s including at least 1 hunger dice creates a messy critical.<br /> <b>- Exploding hunger dice : </b>A hunger die that explode into another success creates a messy critical.<br /> <b>- Messy Exceptional Success :</b> Messy critical happens if any hunger dices are a 10 and the character rolled an exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d probably go with the second option as it makes messy critical wholly reliant on hunger dice chances and doesn\u2019t make more competent character at more risk of getting one, which is IMO the biggest drawback or how messy critical are implemented in v5. I also think exploding dice are really fun in general, and with that rule rolling a 10 on a hunger die would create the risk for a messy critical adding tension after the initial roll instead of the original one. Now instead of rolling and knowing straight away you could get the tensions in some key moments.<br /> <br /> For bestial failure you can probably keep the traditional rule of a failed roll with a 1 on a hunger dice.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a while since I played VTR, so there\u2019s probably some subsystem I haven\u2019t thought about yet, but I\u2019m sure it\u2019s easily manageable. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T04:40:01-07:00","id":1543517,"title":"","content":"Kinda?<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the hungrier you are the harder it is to focus/act like a human as the Beast gnaws on your mind howling to be fed, so overlaying the blood pool with the hunger dice system works for me. Older editions did have rules for getting hungry, but I do like this way.<br /> BP splits into fifths, every one of which has a hunger dice attached (13th gen 2 BP per hunger die, 8th 3 BP per hunger die, etc. Gens 12-9 have an extra buffer before they gain the second dice). Combines the resource management with the theme of being a starving undead cannibal addiction metaphor, and allows generational differences where higher burns out faster but has an easier time filling up and using more humane methods, while lower is a tank who is slow to become hungry and can engage in blood god shenanigans but has a <i>very</i> hard time feeling full when they are hungry: If the antes wake up starving they can drain a human dry and still be on the brink of going into hunger frenzy, hence the fear they'll go cannibalizing the offspring who have a bigger blood pool to snack on.<br /> <br /> I also liked that merit that allowed those with low blood potency to get tattoos and haircuts and manipulated it into older rules. As the blood thins, those above 10th gen begin to lose the stasis that rules vampires. Those older than the Convention of Thorns do call them thinbloods, after all. Some of them even get scars from particularly severe injuries and have to expend extra effort to heal those.<br /> 11th gen can 'heal' piercings, haircuts and tats and etc as bashing.<br /> 12th as lethal.<br /> 13-15th as aggravated.<br /> <br /> I liked the benefits of high humanity with the return of living activities. Technically it exists within humanity as is (free blush of life) but I just have it expand what the blush of life can do for you past sort of being alive for the next eight hours or so. Your reward for redemption is a cookie you can actually eat.<br /> <br /> Also considering convictions and touchstones as backgrounds that make it easier to resist degeneration in your humanity/path if your sins were in situations involving those things. Difficulties to pass the role are lowered by the amount of dots you've invested into that background representing how deeply it matters to you.<br /> Some extra layers of padding for the nightly battle of cognitive dissonance and self-will vs the Beast. On the flip side committing sins in violation of your path <i>and</i> your convictions and touchstones will make the degeneration hit even harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 10-10-2024, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T09:41:10-07:00","id":1543529,"title":"","content":"There's always a steep price to pay for greater power and I do like the blood potency rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T08:15:04-07:00","id":1543582,"title":"","content":"For me, half the problem with Blood Potency x Generation in V5 is the fiddly stuff like &quot;rouse rerolls&quot; and &quot;Discipline bonuses&quot;. I find it needlessly clunky. And most of it is there to simulate having a larger blood pool (or a larger dice pool for elders) without having blood points.<br /> <br /> Classic VTM's &quot;this costs 1 blood point but you might have more than 1 you can spend per turn&quot; (plus scaling trait maximums below 8th Generation) is way simpler and cuts the cruft. Though, making that stuff all equal to (Blood Potency/2) does make it easier to remember, certainly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 10-12-2024, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}